    <string name="stat_ssh_links_detail">%1$d of %2$d SSH connections alive</string>
    <string name="stat_ssh_links_help">Parallel SSH connections to the server. Fewer alive than total means one dropped and is reconnecting — throughput is reduced meanwhile.</string>
    <string name="stat_dial_failures_help">Connections the server could not open to the destination (refused, timed out, or a protocol the server lacks). Occasional increases are normal background noise: dead trackers, apps racing several addresses. A rapid, steady climb points to a real problem. Set the log level to Debug to see each failure with its reason.</string>
    <string name="stat_udp_short">UDP active / dropped</string>
    <string name="stat_udp_help">Without udpgw only DNS travels over UDP. Other UDP (mostly QUIC) is rejected immediately so apps fall back to TCP. If games or calls don’t work, a growing “dropped” count is why.</string>
